From 109eaa656a8d9f0528afb6cbf2ace41b92cb1f59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:29:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 093/112] dsv4 + graph + moe-stream : SiegeLadder C7c - past
 layer 20 the ubatch holding C7's bound runs only its rows from the bound (on
 by default with C7b, LLAMA_DSV4_YOCO_CUT=0 - off; _CUT_MIN - the rows the cut
 must leave, 64). The rows before the bound are C7b's rows without
 consequence: no output, their decoder windows are read by no row past the
 bound (C7's masks), and the state a call leaves is its last rows. Layer 20
 still runs every row (its cache writes are the compressed attention of every
 position; it is also the index and candidate source); from layer 21 the graph
 takes views of the rows [cut, n_tokens): the stream, the carried hc mix,
 layer 20's top-k and candidate verdicts, the positions; the HCA group's
 inputs (masks, the ring's write rows, the dense path's C7 ring mask) are
 views made once per graph, the P13 / D10 plan gets a chunk boundary at the
 cut (only the chunk holding it is split), and the head gathers its outputs at
 their rows past the cut (llm_graph_input_out_ids). The expert stream skips no
 rows past the cut (c7_layer1). Not in the reserve graph, MODE=mask or
 NOBOUND. Checked (SiegeLadder runs.md 4.234-4.235): against C7 computed
 exactly at -ub 1 C7c is no farther than C7b (|d log p| 0.011 against 0.018 on
 3000 / 4500 / 18000-token prompts: dense, P13 chunks, sparse chunks with the
 candidate filter; no argmax flips); agent-long dNLL +0.0002 [-0.0024,
 +0.0027], its per-position difference to C7b (0.022) equal to the pipeline's
 own numeric floor (a FlashAttention tile shift: 0.022). Agent turns 2-8 read
 in 50.7 s against 59.0 s (A B B A, -14%; turn 7.5K -19%)

